\ Strict-mode positive case: a swap over an opaque row keeps its pair concrete. A
\ runtime-depth `drop-at` collapses the stack into a row; pushing a predicate
\ above it and swapping it under the row top leaves both swapped values as
\ concrete entries above a fresh row, so the `loop` in the true arm finds a
\ predicate slot to dispatch rather than the row. This is prelude `loop`'s
\ recursion step, `dup [ call ] dip swap [ loop ] [ drop ] if`, isolated to the
\ swap and the arm that consumes the pair. Under --interpreter-fallback=false the
\ build must succeed and run correctly.
1 2 3 0 drop-at [ 1 - dup 0 > ] swap [ loop ] [ drop ] if .
